    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. The erosion/limestone stuff makes sense, but I'm also looking at the section on seismic activity and soil composition. There's some mention of the soil being highly saturated and loose in certain zones. Does that impact the structural integrity during a minor tremor, or is that just standard stuff we can engineer around?",
